      "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe mainline `DEEPEP_COMMIT` pin (`9af0e0d` = DeepEP v1.2.1, 2025-09-15) predates deepseek-ai/DeepEP#458 (2025-10-17), which added hidden-dim **3072** to the low-latency kernels' `SWITCH_HIDDEN` table. Images built from the current pin abort CUDA-graph capture for hidden=3072 models (e.g. MiniMax-M2 family) when using `--moe-a2a-backend deepep` in low-latency mode:\n\n```\nRuntimeError: Failed: Assertion error /sgl-workspace/DeepEP/csrc/kernels/internode_ll.cu:391 'false and \"Unsupported hidden\"'\n```\n\nContext: #24502 (we hit this on 8× B300 in April; offered to submit this bump there).\n\n## Modifications\n\nTwo-line pin bump, `9af0e0d` → `567632d`:\n\n- `docker/Dockerfile` — `ARG DEEPEP_COMMIT`\n- `scripts/ci/cuda/ci_install_deepep.sh` — matching `git checkout`\n\n**Why `567632d` and not DeepEP main or the #458 merge commit:** `567632d` is the last commit before DeepEP's EPv2 repo reorg (deepseek-ai/DeepEP#605, 2026-04-29), which moved kernels to `csrc/kernels/legacy/` and rewrote `setup.py` — a post-reorg pin breaks this Dockerfile's `csrc/kernels/configs.cuh` sed and build steps. Relative to the #458 merge commit, `567632d` additionally includes the `use_fabric` buffer kwarg (deepseek-ai/DeepEP#217), which sglang passes on CUDA-13 + MNNVL-fabric setups, and NVSHMEM 3.5 runtime fixes (deepseek-ai/DeepEP#564). The `deep_ep` Python API surface between the two pins is strictly additive (diffed `deep_ep/` including `buffer.py` signatures and pybind exports).\n\nOne behavioral note: #458 adds `assert self.nvshmem_qp_depth >= (num_max_dispatch_tokens_per_rank + 1) * 2` in low-latency mode — deployments with a small `NVSHMEM_QP_DEPTH` may need to raise it.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nN/A — build pin only; no model/kernel code changed in sglang.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A. We no longer have Blackwell hardware to build-and-serve validate this image; flagging for CI validation (the GB200/Hopper-SBO variants use separate pins and are untouched).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [ ] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #29561892021](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/29561892021)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #29561891819](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/29561891819)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
